# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every system. The
# tests read the case files, the sources, the justfile and the workflows as
# text: a carriage return that a Windows checkout adds (Git for Windows sets
# `core.autocrlf`) makes every case file refused, since a case line holds no
# raw control character, and the CI job on Windows checks the repository out
# that way. Binary files are found by their content and left as they are.
* text=auto eol=lf
